  "id": "auditory-closure",
  "term": "auditory closure",
  "definition": "Auditory closure is the ability to make sense of speech when parts of the sound are missing or masked by noise. It involves using partial sound cues together with cognitive and language-based top-down processes to reconstruct the intended message.",
